    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's an interesting angle. \"effective initiation of therapeutic action\" sounds pretty strong. \n\nbut i gotta ask—is there actually any clinical evidence that the dizziness is tied to the mechanism of action like that? i haven't seen anything in the internal reports linking the dizziness to rapid absorption or therapeutic onset. if a doctor asks for the specific study that supports that \"transient sign of efficacy\" claim, what are the reps supposed to say? i don't want them getting caught in a lie if they can't back it up with data.",
